  "userDescription": "## Authority\n\nAuthoritative operational record for the complete hotel property estate.\n\n## Use this source for\n\n- Property, room, room-type, amenity, outlet, inventory, and rate facts.\n- Daily operating performance, maintenance requests, and work-order status.\n- Official property names and stable operational business keys.\n\n## Boundary\n\nGuest identity, reservations, stays, folios, payments, disputes, and special requests belong to HotelGuestServices.",
  "dataSourceInstructions": "Use HotelOperations for authoritative property and operational reads; route guest, reservation, and folio questions elsewhere. Join cross-source results with `property_id` and resolve it to the official property name. Data dictionary: `properties` is the property master. Fields: `property_id` is the stable hotel key; `name` is the official display name; `region`, `city`, and `country` locate the property; `currency` is its reporting currency; `tax_rate` is the local hotel tax rate; `facilities` lists on-property facilities; `pool_hours` states pool availability; `parking` contains parking and valet details including stated prices; `transport` contains shuttle and transportation details. `property_daily_metrics` stores daily operating facts. Fields: `service_date` is the business date; `sellable_rooms` and `occupied_rooms` are inventory counts; `room_revenue` is room revenue in property currency. `maintenance_requests` stores reported facilities issues. Fields: `maintenance_request_id` is the request key; `property_id` joins the property; `status` is workflow state; `reported_at` is the report timestamp. `work_orders` stores execution records. Fields: `work_order_id` is the work key; `maintenance_request_id` joins the originating request; `priority` is urgency; `opened_at` is the opening timestamp.",
